{"source": "runtime batch3a b3-circle-s3-point live student run, saved turn (audio urls dropped)", "turn": {"orderIndex": 0, "question": "Does the point (4,2) lie on, inside or outside the circle (x-1)^2+(y+2)^2=25?", "rawResponse": "[STEP]\nThe circle equation is \\((x-1)^2 + (y+2)^2 = 25\\). The center is \\(C(1, -2)\\) and the radius squared is \\(25\\), so the radius equals \\(5\\). [WRITE:Center: \\(C(1, -2)\\), Radius: \\(r = 5\\),90,145]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nTo determine if the point \\((4, 2)\\) lies on, inside, or outside the circle, we calculate the distance from the center \\(C(1, -2)\\) to the point \\((4, 2)\\) and compare it to the radius. [WRITE:Distance formula: \\(d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\\),90,211]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nSubstitute the coordinates of the center and the point into the distance formula. [WRITE:\\(d = \\sqrt{(4 - 1)^2 + (2 - (-2))^2}\\),90,277]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nSimplify the expression inside the square root. [WRITE:\\(d = \\sqrt{(3)^2 + (4)^2}\\),90,343]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nCalculate the squares. [WRITE:\\(d = \\sqrt{9 + 16}\\),90,409]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nAdd the values inside the square root. [WRITE:\\(d = \\sqrt{25}\\),90,475]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nTake the square root. [WRITE:\\(d = 5\\),90,541]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nThe distance from the center to the point is \\(5\\), which is equal to the radius of the circle. [WRITE:Since \\(d = r\\), the point lies on the circle.,90,607]\n[/STEP]\n[STEP]\nTherefore, the point \\((4, 2)\\) lies on the circle. [EMPHASIZE:last]\n[/STEP]", "speedMultiplier": 1.25, "sceneDocument": {"source": {"question": "Does the point (4,2) lie on, inside or outside the circle (x-1)^2+(y+2)^2=25?", "sourceLabel": "question"}, "entities": [{"id": "ax", "kind": "axes", "role": "axes"}, {"id": "C", "kind": "point", "role": "center", "label": "C"}, {"id": "P", "kind": "point", "role": "given_point", "label": "P"}, {"id": "circ", "kind": "circle", "role": "given_circle"}, {"id": "rad", "kind": "segment", "role": "radiu